k an adult to be nearby and stop if anything feels unsafe. You may always describe a choice instead of performing it. One deliberate artistic choice with a named effect is more useful than a longer praise sentence.","icon":"📖","notice":"Repeating the worked example cannot show transfer to a new artwork or performance. Name the element or technique and its effect, not just decoration.","title":"Transfer to a new artwork or performance"}],"title":"Year 4, Week 33, Lesson 1: Stagecraft: sets, lighting and sound","unit_number":7,"unit_title":"Drama: scripts and theatre","week":33,"week_in_unit":3,"word_challenges":null,"worked_example":"WORK THROUGH THIS\nExample: For a storm scene, grey cloth backdrop, torch flickered upward for lightning, drum cue for thunder. Audience reads ''storm'' without explanation.\n\nWrite what makes this example effective, naming the element, technique or performance choice and its effect.","worked_visuals":[{"alt":"Stagecraft tools.","caption":"Serve the story.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Set</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">place story</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Light</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">mood angle</text></g></svg>"},{"alt":"Selective design.","caption":"Less can clarify.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Sound</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">cue meaning</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Clutter</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">avoid ext